Fontconfig and Windows fonts

Install:
  Install missing fontconfig and copy missing Windows fonts when the source is available; refresh the cache after copying.

Upgrade:
  Update installed fontconfig and replace existing Windows font copies when the source is available; refresh the cache after copying.

Status:
  Report the fontconfig package version, copied font count, and source availability.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Source: /mnt/c/Windows/Fonts
  Destination: ~/.local/share/fonts/windows
  Missing source directories are skipped; upgrade does not copy fonts that have not been installed.
